---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import ButtonLink from '../../components/ButtonLink.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="PointPower | Jorge Buckley"
  description="PointPower: a React Native app for planning credit card rewards. Still in progress."
>
  <Container class="space-y-10" width="narrow">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-luxe-accent)] m-0">Public project · In progress</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        PointPower
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        A React Native app I'm building to help plan and maximize credit card rewards, with a small backend behind it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="context-heading">
      <h2 id="context-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Context</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Rewards planning usually means bouncing between issuer sites, spreadsheets, and guesswork. PointPower tries to put the planning flow in one place.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="role-heading">
      <h2 id="role-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Role</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        I'm building the whole thing: React Native client, TypeScript throughout, and a Node/Supabase backend.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="decisions-heading">
      <h2 id="decisions-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        One hard decision
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        I started with planning first, not a giant card catalog. The job is helping someone decide how to use rewards, so the UI leads with goals and scenarios instead of a flat list of every card feature.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="architecture-heading">
      <h2 id="architecture-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        Implementation notes
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        <li>Expo and React Native for the mobile client.</li>
        <li>Zustand for local planning state.</li>
        <li>Supabase for backend services and data.</li>
        <li>TypeScript across the stack so domain models stay clear as things change.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="result-heading">
      <h2 id="result-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Status</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Still in progress. The concept is solid and the foundations work, but this isn't a launched consumer app yet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
      <h2 id="next-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        What I'd improve next
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Better onboarding around one planning scenario, clearer empty and error states, and screenshots once the main flows are stable enough to show.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="tech-heading">
      <h2 id="tech-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Technologies</h2>
      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 list-none m-0 p-0">
        {['Node.js', 'Supabase', 'Expo', 'React Native', 'TypeScript', 'Zustand'].map((tag) => (
          <li class="px-2 py-1 bg-[color:var(--color-luxe-card)] border border-[color:var(--color-luxe-border)] text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)] rounded text-sm">
            {tag}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <ButtonLink
        href="https://github.com/jrbuckley/PointPower"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        umamiEvent="case-pointpower-github"
      >
        View on GitHub
      </ButtonLink>
      <ButtonLink href="/services#react-product" variant="secondary" umamiEvent="case-pointpower-services">
        React product development
      </ButtonLink>
    </div>

    <p>
      <a
        href="/work"
        class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-accent)] hover:underline focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[color:var(--color-luxe-accent)] rounded"
      >
        ← Back to work
      </a>
    </p>
  </Container>
</Layout>
